In the Command design pattern
encapsulate a request as an object and decouple the invoker from the receiver.
we have a command interface
concrete command classes implementing command interface (performing actions)
command invoker which takes the runtime command object and passes it to the concrete command class
class which has to be modified or changed
( main class )

Invoker → Command → Receiver

The important thing about making the request an object is that the request itself can now be stored, passed around,
queued, logged, retried, or undone.
Command turns an action/request into an object, allowing the request to be manipulated independently of the
receiver.